   "id": "erdos902.variants.erdos_lower",
   "module": "OpenProofs.Results.Erdos.P902_erdos_lower",
   "theorem": "OpenProofs.Erdos902.erdos_902.variants.erdos_lower",
   "ref_kind": "upstream",
   "ref_module": "FormalConjectures.ErdosProblems.«902»",
   "ref_theorem": "Erdos902.erdos_902.variants.erdos_lower",
   "tier": "a",
   "assessment": "proved",
   "summary": "Erdős [Er63c]: f(n) ≥ 2^(n+1) − 1.",
   "notes": "Because f is an sInf over ℕ (0 if no tournament has property S_n), the formal statement also asserts that S_n tournaments exist for every n; the proof covers both: the in-neighbourhood recursion f(n) ≥ 2f(n−1)+1 and Erdős's probabilistic existence argument as a counting/union bound. Not a misformalization (both parts are true and due to Erdős), but the statement is stronger than the informal lower bound alone."
  },
